{"name":"Calla Lily","hex":"#e4eaed","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calla lily","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common name for certain flowering plants in the genus Zantedeschia; not related to either the genus Calla or the true lilies (Liliaceae)","A flower of one of these plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calla_lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calla lily","blocks":[{"text":"Calla lily is a common name of several members of the family, Araceae. It may refer to:"},{"items":["Calla palustris","Zantedeschia generally\nZantedeschia aethiopica specifically","Zantedeschia aethiopica specifically"]},{"items":["Zantedeschia aethiopica specifically"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla_lily","wikidata":"Q28699150"},{"title":"Calla Lily (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Calla Lily is a 2006 Philippine television drama series broadcast by ABS-CBN. Directed by Maryo J. de los Reyes and Lino Cayetano, it stars Sharlene San Pedro in the title role. It aired on the network's Primetime Bida line up from May 29 to September 8, 2006, replacing Panday and was replaced by Crazy for You."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla_Lily_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q5021698"},{"title":"Calla","blocks":[{"text":"Calla is a genus of flowering plant in the family Araceae, containing the single species Calla palustris. It is the only genus in the tribe Calleae of the subfamily Aroideae. Its systematic position has been described as \"puzzling\", and it has also been placed in its own family Callaceae and its own subfamily Calloideae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Calla_palustris2.jpg/330px-Calla_palustris2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla","wikidata":"Q1945962"},{"title":"Zantedeschia","blocks":[{"text":"Zantedeschia is a genus of eight species of herbaceous, perennial, flowering plants in the aroid fa